{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>It and its offspring</b> — twice here, and the other: \"and serve him\" etc. \"and its offspring\" concerning Nebuchadnezzar, because it is stated: \"it and its offspring you shall not slaughter on one day,\" and he did not do so, but slaughtered the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes. Therefore it is stated of him: \"and serve him and his offspring until the time of his land come; he and his offspring shall serve in it many nations\" — that Belshazzar killed him and the kingdom was taken from him. \"It and its offspring\" is juxtaposed to \"ox or sheep\" to teach that it applies to consecrated animals."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:18.318050837Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}